Simorgh Channels — notice file
==============================

This repository is the curated registry of public Telegram channels that
post free proxy configurations, used by the Simorgh macOS project's
server-discovery harvest (see HELBOYCODER/simorgh-servers).

The channel registry concept is taken from zeghostwriter/ZeroNet
(https://github.com/zeghostwriter/ZeroNet, MIT License — Copyright (c)
zeghostwriter/ZeroNet contributors; full text quoted in
https://github.com/HELBOYCODER/simorgh-servers/blob/main/NOTICE), whose
`deploy/crowd/telegram-channels.json` seed list is reproduced here under the
Simorgh brand.

The channels listed are independent third-party Telegram channels. Simorgh
reads their public web pages (t.me/s/<name>) the way a browser would. The
project does not operate, review, or endorse any channel or any configuration
posted in one; every config harvested from a channel is tested before it can
reach a user, and a channel that stops posting is dropped by the harvest.
